/-!
# Checked source-conjugacy trees for the finite census pairs

Pruned trees cover the independent four-groups occurring in all literal rows
and the five extra pure sixteens. Edges apply the original max2 X or Y, followed
by a change of basis in the same four-group. The arithmetic uses the existing
proved thirteen-bit multiplication and source action. These certificates do
not assert ranks; RankTransport applies the four separately proved roots.
Source: Kleidman--Wilson (1988), pp.488--489, and ATLAS J4G1-max2W1.
-/
